# Use with VS Code REST Client or Visual Studio (.http). Start the API first: dotnet run --project src/AiOralExam.Api
@host = http://localhost:5080

# Sign-in happens in Keycloak (password grant is disabled), so get a token through Swagger:
# http://localhost:5080/swagger -> Authorize -> sign in as han.hg@aives.edu.vn / Password@123,
# run any request and copy the token from the "Authorization: Bearer ..." header of the shown curl command.
# Tokens expire after 5 minutes.
@token = paste-access-token-here

### My exam sessions
GET {{host}}/api/interview/my-sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update my profile (own account)
PATCH {{host}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "Updated Full Name" }

### Start an attempt (SWD392 session, currently open)
POST {{host}}/api/interview-attempts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "examSessionId": "33333333-0000-0000-0000-000000000001" }

### Submit an answer (replace ATTEMPT_ID)
POST {{host}}/api/interview-attempts/ATTEMPT_ID/responses
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "turnId": "CURRENT_TURN_ID", "answerText": "A modular monolith is deployed as one unit but split into business modules; each module owns its tables and talks to the others only through interfaces." }

### Submit an audio answer (replace ATTEMPT_ID and CURRENT_TURN_ID)
POST {{host}}/api/interview-attempts/ATTEMPT_ID/audio
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=audioBoundary

--audioBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="turnId"

CURRENT_TURN_ID
--audioBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="answer.webm"
Content-Type: audio/webm

< ./answer.webm
--audioBoundary--

### List course materials (lecturer/admin token; replace COURSE_ID)
GET {{host}}/api/courses/COURSE_ID/materials
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Upload a private course source file (replace COURSE_ID)
POST {{host}}/api/courses/COURSE_ID/materials
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=materialBoundary

--materialBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="rag-source.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

Retrieval augmented generation uses course-scoped evidence and citation labels.
--materialBoundary--

### Ingest the uploaded material (replace COURSE_ID and MATERIAL_ID)
POST {{host}}/api/courses/COURSE_ID/materials/MATERIAL_ID/ingest
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Generate reviewable F1 drafts (replace COURSE_ID and RUBRIC_VERSION_ID)
POST {{host}}/api/courses/COURSE_ID/question-bank/generations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "topic": "Retrieval augmented generation",
  "bloom": "Understand",
  "count": 2,
  "sourceExcerpts": ["Retrieval selects relevant chunks before generation."],
  "sourceMaterialIds": [],
  "platformRubricVersionId": "RUBRIC_VERSION_ID"
}

### List Draft question-bank items (replace COURSE_ID)
GET {{host}}/api/courses/COURSE_ID/question-bank?status=Draft
Authorization: ******

### Create a manual question-bank Draft (replace COURSE_ID)
POST {{host}}/api/courses/COURSE_ID/question-bank
Authorization: ******
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "topic": "Relational databases",
  "bloom": "Understand",
  "content": "Explain the purpose of a primary key."
}

### Import question-bank Drafts (replace COURSE_ID)
POST {{host}}/api/courses/COURSE_ID/question-bank/import
Authorization: ******
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [
    {
      "topic": "Relational databases",
      "bloom": "Remember",
      "content": "Define a relation."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Relational databases",
      "bloom": "Apply",
      "content": "Choose a primary key for a student table."
    }
  ]
}

### Invalid bank import (expects 400 with row/field details)
POST {{host}}/api/courses/COURSE_ID/question-bank/import
Authorization: ******
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [
    {
      "topic": "Relational databases",
      "bloom": "Remember",
      "content": " "
    }
  ]
}

### Get a question-bank item and its revisions (replace COURSE_ID and ITEM_ID)
GET {{host}}/api/courses/COURSE_ID/question-bank/ITEM_ID
Authorization: ******

### Edit a Draft and create a revision (replace COURSE_ID and ITEM_ID)
PUT {{host}}/api/courses/COURSE_ID/question-bank/ITEM_ID
Authorization: ******
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "topic": "Relational databases",
  "bloom": "Analyze",
  "content": "Compare candidate keys and primary keys."
}

### Approve a Draft (replace COURSE_ID and ITEM_ID)
POST {{host}}/api/courses/COURSE_ID/question-bank/ITEM_ID/approve
Authorization: ******

### Reject a Draft (replace COURSE_ID and ITEM_ID)
POST {{host}}/api/courses/COURSE_ID/question-bank/ITEM_ID/reject
Authorization: ******

### Attach Approved items to a Draft session (replace SESSION_ID and item IDs)
POST {{host}}/api/exam-sessions/SESSION_ID/questions/from-bank
Authorization: ******
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "itemIds": ["ITEM_ID_1", "ITEM_ID_2"]
}

### Health check
GET {{host}}/health

### Create a user (administrator)
POST {{host}}/api/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Han Hoang Giang",
  "email": "new.student@aives.edu.vn",
  "role": "Student",
  "studentCode": "SE180099",
  "lecturerCode": null
}

### Resend a user's password setup email (administrator; replace USER_ID)
POST {{host}}/api/admin/users/USER_ID/setup-link
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
